doc:sec-15ra-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "15RA(1) Meanings of road transport contractual chain and in a road" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) A road transport contractual chain means a chain or series of contracts or arrangements: (a) under which work is performed for a party to the first contract or arrangement in the chain or series by a regulated road transport contractor or a road transport employee-like worker under a services contract, or by an employee; and (b) in which at least one party to the first contract or arrangement in the chain or series is a constitutional corporation." ;
    cof:pageNumber "107"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-15ra-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "15RA(2) Meanings of road transport contractual chain and in a road"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-15ra-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) A person is in a road transport contractual chain if: (a) the person is a party (a primary party) to the first contract or arrangement in the road transport contractual chain; or (b) the person is a party (a secondary party) to a subsequent contract or arrangement in the road transport contractual chain, being a contract or arrangement under which work is performed for the secondary party by a regulated road  Chapter 1  Introduction" ;
    skos:definition "(2) A person is in a road transport contractual chain if: (a) the person is a party (a primary party) to the first contract or arrangement in the road transport contractual chain; or (b) the person is a party (a secondary party) to a subsequent contract or arrangement in the road transport contractual chain, being a contract or arrangement under which work is performed for the secondary party by a regulated road  Chapter 1  Introduction"@en ;
