doc:sec-20-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "20(1) Meaning of ordinary hours of work for award/agreement free" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) The ordinary hours of work of an award/agreement free employee are the hours agreed by the employee and his or her national system employer as the employee’s ordinary hours of work. If there is no agreement" ;
    cof:pageNumber "117"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-20-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "20(2) Meaning of ordinary hours of work for award/agreement free"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-20-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) If there is no agreement about ordinary hours of work for an award/agreement free employee, the ordinary hours of work of the employee in a week are: (a) for a full-time employee—38 hours; or (b) for an employee who is not a full-time employee—the lesser of: (i) 38 hours; and (ii) the employee’s usual weekly hours of work.  Chapter 1  Introduction" ;
    skos:definition "(2) If there is no agreement about ordinary hours of work for an award/agreement free employee, the ordinary hours of work of the employee in a week are: (a) for a full-time employee—38 hours; or (b) for an employee who is not a full-time employee—the lesser of: (i) 38 hours; and (ii) the employee’s usual weekly hours of work.  Chapter 1  Introduction"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b64d28f06f81e7b813ab2d78020343286e7b49ae11fe8e5117cfdf729df9430d" ;
