concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-23 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "23 Meaning of small business employer"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-23 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A national system employer is a small business employer at a particular time if the employer employs fewer than 15 employees at that time. (2) For the purpose of calculating the number of employees employed by the employer at a particular time: (a) subject to paragraph (b), all employees employed by the employer at that time are to be counted; and (b) a casual employee is not to be counted unless, at that time, the employee is a regular casual employee of the employer. (3) For the purpose of calculating the number of employees employed by the employer at a particular time, associated entities are taken to be one entity.  Introduction  Chapter 1 Definitions  Part 1-2 Other definitions  Division 4 Section 23A Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 (4) To avoid doubt, in determining whether a national system employer is a small business employer at a particular time in relation to the dismissal of an employee, or termination of an employee’s employment, the employees that are to be counted include (subject to paragraph (2)(b)): (a) the employee who is being dismissed or whose employment is being terminated; and (b) any other employee of the employer who is also being dismissed or whose employment is also being terminated." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A national system employer is a small business employer at a particular time if the employer employs fewer than 15 employees at that time. (2) For the purpose of calculating the number of employees employed by the employer at a particular time: (a) subject to paragraph (b), all employees employed by the employer at that time are to be counted; and (b) a casual employee is not to be counted unless, at that time, the employee is a regular casual employee of the employer. (3) For the purpose of calculating the number of employees employed by the employer at a particular time, associated entities are taken to be one entity.  Introduction  Chapter 1 Definitions  Part 1-2 Other definitions  Division 4 Section 23A Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 (4) To avoid doubt, in determining whether a national system employer is a small business employer at a particular time in relation to the dismissal of an employee, or termination of an employee’s employment, the employees that are to be counted include (subject to paragraph (2)(b)): (a) the employee who is being dismissed or whose employment is being terminated; and (b) any other employee of the employer who is also being dismissed or whose employment is also being terminated."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "547a6e9c65f1d0c9dd043082808386b1f6dd73b089917c44e4e2561d4452eba0" ;
    cof:pageNumber "122"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-23-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-23-ss-2 ;
