concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-23a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "23A Terms relating to superannuation"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-23a ;
    values:originalText "(1) MySuper product has the meaning given by the Superannuation Industry (Supervision) Act 1993. (1A) A standard MySuper product is a MySuper product that is not an employer MySuper product. (1B) An employer MySuper product is a tailored MySuper product or a corporate MySuper product. (2) A tailored MySuper product is a MySuper product in relation to which section 29TB of the Superannuation Industry (Supervision) Act 1993 is satisfied. (3) A corporate MySuper product is a MySuper product that is offered by a superannuation fund that: (a) is a standard employer-sponsored fund (within the meaning of the Superannuation Industry (Supervision) Act 1993); and (b) is not a public offer superannuation fund (within the meaning of that Act); and (c) has: (i) one standard employer-sponsor (within the meaning of that Act); or (ii) 2 or more standard employer-sponsors (within the meaning of that Act) that are associates of each other for the purposes of that Act.  Chapter 1  Introduction" ;
    skos:definition "(1) MySuper product has the meaning given by the Superannuation Industry (Supervision) Act 1993. (1A) A standard MySuper product is a MySuper product that is not an employer MySuper product. (1B) An employer MySuper product is a tailored MySuper product or a corporate MySuper product. (2) A tailored MySuper product is a MySuper product in relation to which section 29TB of the Superannuation Industry (Supervision) Act 1993 is satisfied. (3) A corporate MySuper product is a MySuper product that is offered by a superannuation fund that: (a) is a standard employer-sponsored fund (within the meaning of the Superannuation Industry (Supervision) Act 1993); and (b) is not a public offer superannuation fund (within the meaning of that Act); and (c) has: (i) one standard employer-sponsor (within the meaning of that Act); or (ii) 2 or more standard employer-sponsors (within the meaning of that Act) that are associates of each other for the purposes of that Act.  Chapter 1  Introduction"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "915c12dd9b08c4fb80f071c486d24f8f1d830c95e9133de1f038cc1912e2fb2c" ;
    cof:pageNumber "123"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-23a-ss-1 ;
