    values:originalText "This Part has the core provisions for this Chapter, which deals with terms and conditions of employment of national system employees. The main terms and conditions come from the National Employment Standards, modern awards, enterprise agreements and workplace determinations. The National Employment Standards (Part 2-2) are minimum terms and conditions that apply to all national system employees. A modern award (see Part 2-3), an enterprise agreement (see" ;
    cof:pageNumber "170"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-42 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "42 Meanings of employee and employer"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-42 ;
    values:originalText "In this Part, employee means a national system employee, and employer means a national system employer. Note: See also Division 2 of Part 6-4A (TCF contract outworkers taken to be employees in certain circumstances).  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment" ;
    skos:definition "In this Part, employee means a national system employee, and employer means a national system employer. Note: See also Division 2 of Part 6-4A (TCF contract outworkers taken to be employees in certain circumstances).  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment"@en ;
