concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-51 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "51 The significance of an enterprise agreement applying to a person"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-51 ;
    values:originalText "(1) An enterprise agreement does not impose obligations on a person, and a person does not contravene a term of an enterprise agreement, unless the agreement applies to the person. (2) An enterprise agreement does not give a person an entitlement unless the agreement applies to the person. 52  When an enterprise agreement applies to an employer, employee or employee organisation When an enterprise agreement applies to an employee, employer or organisation (1) An enterprise agreement applies to an employee, employer or employee organisation if: (a) the agreement is in operation; and (b) the agreement covers the employee, employer or organisation; and  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment" ;
    skos:definition "(1) An enterprise agreement does not impose obligations on a person, and a person does not contravene a term of an enterprise agreement, unless the agreement applies to the person. (2) An enterprise agreement does not give a person an entitlement unless the agreement applies to the person. 52  When an enterprise agreement applies to an employer, employee or employee organisation When an enterprise agreement applies to an employee, employer or organisation (1) An enterprise agreement applies to an employee, employer or employee organisation if: (a) the agreement is in operation; and (b) the agreement covers the employee, employer or organisation; and  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "2b1be630831802e43376bc8014455089db9e7dfda80a523c755745f9906875f4" ;
    cof:pageNumber "177"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-51-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-51-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-51-ss-1 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
