concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-57a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "57A Designated outworker terms of a modern award continue to"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-57a ;
    values:originalText "apply (1) This section applies if, at a particular time: (a) an enterprise agreement applies to an employer; and (b) a modern award covers the employer (whether the modern award covers the employer in the employer’s capacity as an employer or an outworker entity); and (c) the modern award includes one or more designated outworker terms. (2) Despite section 57, the designated outworker terms of the modern award apply at that time to the following: (a) the employer; (b) each employee who is both: (i) a person to whom the enterprise agreement applies; and (ii) a person who is covered by the modern award; (c) each employee organisation that is covered by the modern award. (3) To avoid doubt:  Terms and conditions of employment  Chapter 2 Core provisions for this Chapter  Part 2-1 Interaction between the National Employment Standards, modern awards and enterprise agreements  Division 3 Section 58 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 (a) designated outworker terms of a modern award can apply to an employer under subsection (2) even if none of the employees of the employer is an outworker; and (b) to the extent to which designated outworker terms of a modern award apply to an employer, an employee or an employee organisation because of subsection (2), the modern award applies to the employer, employee or organisation. Subdivision C—Interaction between one or more enterprise agreements" ;
    skos:definition "apply (1) This section applies if, at a particular time: (a) an enterprise agreement applies to an employer; and (b) a modern award covers the employer (whether the modern award covers the employer in the employer’s capacity as an employer or an outworker entity); and (c) the modern award includes one or more designated outworker terms. (2) Despite section 57, the designated outworker terms of the modern award apply at that time to the following: (a) the employer; (b) each employee who is both: (i) a person to whom the enterprise agreement applies; and (ii) a person who is covered by the modern award; (c) each employee organisation that is covered by the modern award. (3) To avoid doubt:  Terms and conditions of employment  Chapter 2 Core provisions for this Chapter  Part 2-1 Interaction between the National Employment Standards, modern awards and enterprise agreements  Division 3 Section 58 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 (a) designated outworker terms of a modern award can apply to an employer under subsection (2) even if none of the employees of the employer is an outworker; and (b) to the extent to which designated outworker terms of a modern award apply to an employer, an employee or an employee organisation because of subsection (2), the modern award applies to the employer, employee or organisation. Subdivision C—Interaction between one or more enterprise agreements"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "97a5e41b45ddd2b2381046e77ccfa5c45d3553b81b66aeba7ed5c460c660f93f" ;
    cof:pageNumber "184"^^xsd:integer ;
