doc:sec-57a-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "57A(3) Designated outworker terms of a modern award continue to" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) To avoid doubt:  Terms and conditions of employment  Chapter 2 Core provisions for this Chapter  Part 2-1 Interaction between the National Employment Standards, modern awards and enterprise agreements  Division 3 Section 58 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 (a) designated outworker terms of a modern award can apply to an employer under subsection (2) even if none of the employees of the employer is an outworker; and (b) to the extent to which designated outworker terms of a modern award apply to an employer, an employee or an employee organisation because of subsection (2), the modern award applies to the employer, employee or organisation. Subdivision C—Interaction between one or more enterprise agreements" ;
    cof:pageNumber "184"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-58 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "58 Only one enterprise agreement can apply to an employee"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-58 ;
    values:originalText "Only one enterprise agreement can apply to an employee (1) Only one enterprise agreement can apply to an employee at a particular time. General rule—later agreement does not apply until earlier agreement passes its nominal expiry date (2) If: (a) an enterprise agreement (the earlier agreement) applies to an employee in relation to particular employment; and (b) another enterprise agreement (the later agreement) that covers the employee in relation to the same employment comes into operation; and (c) subsections (3), (4) and (5) do not apply; then: (d) if the earlier agreement has not passed its nominal expiry date: (i) the later agreement cannot apply to the employee in relation to that employment until the earlier agreement passes its nominal expiry date; and (ii) the earlier agreement ceases to apply to the employee in relation to that employment when the earlier agreement  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment" ;
    skos:definition "Only one enterprise agreement can apply to an employee (1) Only one enterprise agreement can apply to an employee at a particular time. General rule—later agreement does not apply until earlier agreement passes its nominal expiry date (2) If: (a) an enterprise agreement (the earlier agreement) applies to an employee in relation to particular employment; and (b) another enterprise agreement (the later agreement) that covers the employee in relation to the same employment comes into operation; and (c) subsections (3), (4) and (5) do not apply; then: (d) if the earlier agreement has not passed its nominal expiry date: (i) the later agreement cannot apply to the employee in relation to that employment until the earlier agreement passes its nominal expiry date; and (ii) the earlier agreement ceases to apply to the employee in relation to that employment when the earlier agreement  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b0f422cd98f0ee2b3b5a5f0f297f29fc49a4718f22ce33a4e104ef2abaa4547c" ;
    cof:pageNumber "185"^^xsd:integer ;
