doc:sec-65-ss-1b a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "65(1B) Requests for flexible working arrangements" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1B) To avoid doubt, and without limiting subsection (1), an employee who: (a) is a parent, or has responsibility for the care, of a child; and (b) is returning to work after taking leave in relation to the birth or adoption of the child;  Terms and conditions of employment  Chapter 2 The National Employment Standards  Part 2-2 Requests for flexible working arrangements  Division 4 Section 65A Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 may request to work part-time to assist the employee to care for the child." ;
    cof:pageNumber "194"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-65-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "65(2) Requests for flexible working arrangements"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-65-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) The employee is not entitled to make the request unless: (a) for an employee other than a casual employee—the employee has completed at least 12 months of continuous service with the employer immediately before making the request; or (b) for a casual employee—the employee: (i) is, immediately before making the request, a regular casual employee of the employer who has been employed on that basis for a sequence of periods of employment during a period of at least 12 months; and (ii) has a reasonable expectation of continuing employment by the employer on a regular and systematic basis." ;
    skos:definition "(2) The employee is not entitled to make the request unless: (a) for an employee other than a casual employee—the employee has completed at least 12 months of continuous service with the employer immediately before making the request; or (b) for a casual employee—the employee: (i) is, immediately before making the request, a regular casual employee of the employer who has been employed on that basis for a sequence of periods of employment during a period of at least 12 months; and (ii) has a reasonable expectation of continuing employment by the employer on a regular and systematic basis."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "6346ce946bbc1a7c057bc18e8f4effaee8ed7c2a4f3c72d3718838df7b3c8bdd" ;
    values:partOf concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-65 ;
    cof:pageNumber "194"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Request for flexible working arrangements requires minimum service period or regular casual employment" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <fair-work-act-2009.pdf> ;
    dc:source "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.194" ;
