    values:originalText "(1) An employer must not do any of the following in order to avoid any right or obligation under this Division: (a) reduce or vary an employee’s hours of work; (b) change the employee’s pattern of work; (c) terminate an employee’s employment. Note: The general protections provisions in Part 3-1 also prohibit the taking of adverse action by an employer against an employee (which includes a casual employee) because of a workplace right of the employee under this Division." ;
