concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-66ma-ss-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "66MA(5) Arbitration"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-66ma-ss-5 ;
    values:originalText "(5) In considering whether to make, and the terms of, an order under subsection (1) (including an order referred to in subsection (4)) in relation to a dispute about the operation of Subdivision B of this Division (which deals with employee choice about casual employment), the FWC must: (a) have regard to whether substantial changes to the employee’s terms and conditions would be reasonably necessary to ensure the employer does not contravene a term of a fair work instrument that would apply to the employee as a full-time employee or part-time employee; and (b) disregard conduct of the employer and employee that occurred after the employee gave the notification under section 66AAB (which deals with employee choice notifications) to the employer.  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment" ;
    skos:definition "(5) In considering whether to make, and the terms of, an order under subsection (1) (including an order referred to in subsection (4)) in relation to a dispute about the operation of Subdivision B of this Division (which deals with employee choice about casual employment), the FWC must: (a) have regard to whether substantial changes to the employee’s terms and conditions would be reasonably necessary to ensure the employer does not contravene a term of a fair work instrument that would apply to the employee as a full-time employee or part-time employee; and (b) disregard conduct of the employer and employee that occurred after the employee gave the notification under section 66AAB (which deals with employee choice notifications) to the employer.  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "feafcd7ac5c874f6f10bfc063a5163ed325716069fb6e4fef7b14dc982de718d" ;
