concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-68 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "68 General rule for adoption-related leave—child must be under 16"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-68 ;
    values:originalText "etc. An employee is not entitled to adoption-related leave unless the child that is, or is to be, placed with the employee for adoption: (a) is, or will be, under 16 as at the day of placement, or the expected day of placement, of the child; and (b) has not, or will not have, lived continuously with the employee for a period of 6 months or more as at the day of placement, or the expected day of placement, of the child; and (c) is not (otherwise than because of the adoption) a child of the employee or the employee’s spouse or de facto partner." ;
    skos:definition "etc. An employee is not entitled to adoption-related leave unless the child that is, or is to be, placed with the employee for adoption: (a) is, or will be, under 16 as at the day of placement, or the expected day of placement, of the child; and (b) has not, or will not have, lived continuously with the employee for a period of 6 months or more as at the day of placement, or the expected day of placement, of the child; and (c) is not (otherwise than because of the adoption) a child of the employee or the employee’s spouse or de facto partner."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "f6e688bef865198ab4f91e8564a9d4f3c354e244b1ba0c6ec7475c1e9e3a9e7d" ;
    cof:pageNumber "213"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Eligibility for adoption-related leave based on child's age and residency." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <fair-work-act-2009.pdf> ;
    dc:source "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.213" ;
    cml:asserts concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-68-norm .
