doc:sec-68 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "68 General rule for adoption-related leave—child must be under 16" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "etc. An employee is not entitled to adoption-related leave unless the child that is, or is to be, placed with the employee for adoption: (a) is, or will be, under 16 as at the day of placement, or the expected day of placement, of the child; and (b) has not, or will not have, lived continuously with the employee for a period of 6 months or more as at the day of placement, or the expected day of placement, of the child; and (c) is not (otherwise than because of the adoption) a child of the employee or the employee’s spouse or de facto partner." ;
    cof:pageNumber "213"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-69 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "69 Transfer of employment situations in which employee is entitled"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-69 ;
    values:originalText "to continue on leave etc. (1) If: (a) there is a transfer of employment in relation to an employee; and (b) the employee has already started a period of leave under this Division when the employee’s employment with the first employer ends; the employee is entitled to continue on that leave for the rest of that period. (2) If: (a) there is a transfer of employment in relation to an employee; and (b) the employee has, in relation to the first employer, already taken a step that is required or permitted by a provision of this Division in relation to taking a period of leave; the employee is taken to have taken the step in relation to the second employer. Note: Steps covered by this subsection include (for example) complying with a notice or evidence requirement of section 74 in relation to the first employer.  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment" ;
    skos:definition "to continue on leave etc. (1) If: (a) there is a transfer of employment in relation to an employee; and (b) the employee has already started a period of leave under this Division when the employee’s employment with the first employer ends; the employee is entitled to continue on that leave for the rest of that period. (2) If: (a) there is a transfer of employment in relation to an employee; and (b) the employee has, in relation to the first employer, already taken a step that is required or permitted by a provision of this Division in relation to taking a period of leave; the employee is taken to have taken the step in relation to the second employer. Note: Steps covered by this subsection include (for example) complying with a notice or evidence requirement of section 74 in relation to the first employer.  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "adc1aca3039d6f3f602787786769112904f05a57d89037dfb156ebee0ba5e706" ;
    cof:pageNumber "213"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-69-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-69-ss-2 ;
