concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-74-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "74(4) Notice and evidence requirements"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-74-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) If any of the leave covered by the notice is to be taken under section 71, then at least 4 weeks before the intended start date specified in the notice given under subsection (1), the employee must: (a) confirm the intended start and end dates of the leave to be taken under section 71; or (b) advise the employer of any changes to the intended start and end dates of the leave to be taken under section 71;  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment" ;
    skos:definition "(4) If any of the leave covered by the notice is to be taken under section 71, then at least 4 weeks before the intended start date specified in the notice given under subsection (1), the employee must: (a) confirm the intended start and end dates of the leave to be taken under section 71; or (b) advise the employer of any changes to the intended start and end dates of the leave to be taken under section 71;  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "17773ccac499fb3e204c9ebbaab4d3afc44cc9def4366a044962b84df6a40588" ;
    values:partOf concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-74 ;
