concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-75 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "75 Extending period of unpaid parental leave—extending to use"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-75 ;
    values:originalText "more of available parental leave period Application of this section (1) This section applies if: (a) an employee has, in accordance with section 74, given notice of the taking of a period of unpaid parental leave (the original leave period) under section 71; and (b) the original leave period is less than the employee’s available parental leave period; and (c) the original leave period has started. (2) The employee’s available parental leave period is 12 months, less any periods of the following kinds: (b) a period of unpaid parental leave that the employee has been required to take under subsection 73(2) or 82(2); (d) if the employee has given notice in accordance with subsection 74(2) or (2A) of the taking of flexible unpaid  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment" ;
    skos:definition "more of available parental leave period Application of this section (1) This section applies if: (a) an employee has, in accordance with section 74, given notice of the taking of a period of unpaid parental leave (the original leave period) under section 71; and (b) the original leave period is less than the employee’s available parental leave period; and (c) the original leave period has started. (2) The employee’s available parental leave period is 12 months, less any periods of the following kinds: (b) a period of unpaid parental leave that the employee has been required to take under subsection 73(2) or 82(2); (d) if the employee has given notice in accordance with subsection 74(2) or (2A) of the taking of flexible unpaid  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "e078c0d3607f6b8c700a77c6b21dc06374996f0b504b7787f7b49fa819737f47" ;
    cof:pageNumber "223"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-75-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-75-ss-2 ;
