doc:sec-76-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "76(1) Extending period of unpaid parental leave—extending for up to" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) An employee who takes unpaid parental leave under section 71 for the employee’s available parental leave period may request the employee’s employer to agree to an extension of unpaid parental leave for the employee for a further period of up to 12 months immediately following the end of the available parental leave period. Note: Extended periods of unpaid parental leave can include keeping in touch days on which an employee performs work (see section 79A).  Terms and conditions of employment  Chapter 2 The National Employment Standards  Part 2-2 Parental leave and related entitlements  Division 5 Section 76A Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 Making the request" ;
    cof:pageNumber "224"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-76-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "76(2) Extending period of unpaid parental leave—extending for up to"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-76-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) The request must be in writing, and must be given to the employer at least 4 weeks before the end of the available parental leave period. Note: The request must be made when the employee is taking unpaid parental leave under section 71. No extension beyond 24 months after birth or placement" ;
    skos:definition "(2) The request must be in writing, and must be given to the employer at least 4 weeks before the end of the available parental leave period. Note: The request must be made when the employee is taking unpaid parental leave under section 71. No extension beyond 24 months after birth or placement"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "395a55afc9df4ae91d28abec6079186fab0568529ad59a646ba1efc40125064a" ;
    values:partOf concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-76 ;
    cof:pageNumber "224"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Employer must receive written request for extension of unpaid parental leave at least 4 weeks before the end of the available period." ;
    dc:description "Written request" ;
