concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-78-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "78(3) Employee who ceases to have responsibility for care of child"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-78-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) The specified day: (a) must be at least 4 weeks after the notice is given to the employee; and  Terms and conditions of employment  Chapter 2 The National Employment Standards  Part 2-2 Parental leave and related entitlements  Division 5 Section 78A Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 (b) if the leave is birth-related leave taken by an employee who has given birth—must not be earlier than 6 weeks after the date of birth of the child." ;
    skos:definition "(3) The specified day: (a) must be at least 4 weeks after the notice is given to the employee; and  Terms and conditions of employment  Chapter 2 The National Employment Standards  Part 2-2 Parental leave and related entitlements  Division 5 Section 78A Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 (b) if the leave is birth-related leave taken by an employee who has given birth—must not be earlier than 6 weeks after the date of birth of the child."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "a27d140005f7abd3723dc2b083c877797ff8ac0c0cd29b67ac73541ef9900dbc" ;
    values:partOf concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-78 ;
    cof:pageNumber "232"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Employee must provide at least 4 weeks' notice before ceasing responsibility for child care." ;
    dc:description "Notice" ;
