concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-79b a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "79B Unpaid parental leave not extended by paid leave or keeping in"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-79b ;
    values:originalText "touch days If, during a period of unpaid parental leave, an employee: (a) takes paid leave; or (b) performs work for the employee’s employer on a keeping in touch day; taking that leave or performing that work does not have the effect of extending the period of unpaid parental leave. Subdivision C—Other entitlements" ;
    skos:definition "touch days If, during a period of unpaid parental leave, an employee: (a) takes paid leave; or (b) performs work for the employee’s employer on a keeping in touch day; taking that leave or performing that work does not have the effect of extending the period of unpaid parental leave. Subdivision C—Other entitlements"@en ;
