doc:sec-91-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "91(1) Transfer of employment situations that affect entitlement to" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) Subsection 22(5) does not apply (for the purpose of this Division) to a transfer of employment between non-associated entities in relation to an employee, if the second employer decides not to  Terms and conditions of employment  Chapter 2 The National Employment Standards  Part 2-2 Annual leave  Division 6 Section 92 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 recognise the employee’s service with the first employer (for the purpose of this Division). Employee is not entitled to payment for untaken annual leave if service with first employer counts as service with second employer" ;
    cof:pageNumber "246"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-91-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "91(2) Transfer of employment situations that affect entitlement to"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-91-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) If subsection 22(5) applies (for the purpose of this Division) to a transfer of employment in relation to an employee, the employee is not entitled to be paid an amount under subsection 90(2) for a period of untaken paid annual leave. Note: Subsection 22(5) provides that, generally, if there is a transfer of employment, service with the first employer counts as service with the second employer." ;
    skos:definition "(2) If subsection 22(5) applies (for the purpose of this Division) to a transfer of employment in relation to an employee, the employee is not entitled to be paid an amount under subsection 90(2) for a period of untaken paid annual leave. Note: Subsection 22(5) provides that, generally, if there is a transfer of employment, service with the first employer counts as service with the second employer."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "21d21c106901e2410e440618aafcc16378a5c39fac933948c8b3311601a7ede6" ;
    values:partOf concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-91 ;
