doc:sec-94-ss-4 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "94(4) Cashing out and taking paid annual leave for award/agreement" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(4) The employer must pay the employee at least the full amount that would have been payable to the employee had the employee taken the leave that the employee has forgone.  Terms and conditions of employment  Chapter 2 The National Employment Standards  Part 2-2 Annual leave  Division 6 Section 94 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 Requirements to take paid annual leave" ;
    cof:pageNumber "248"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-94-ss-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "94(5) Cashing out and taking paid annual leave for award/agreement"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-94-ss-5 ;
    values:originalText "(5) An employer may require an award/agreement free employee to take a period of paid annual leave, but only if the requirement is reasonable. Note: A requirement to take paid annual leave may be reasonable if, for example: (a) the employee has accrued an excessive amount of paid annual leave; or (b) the employer’s enterprise is being shut down for a period (for example, between Christmas and New Year). Agreements about taking paid annual leave" ;
    skos:definition "(5) An employer may require an award/agreement free employee to take a period of paid annual leave, but only if the requirement is reasonable. Note: A requirement to take paid annual leave may be reasonable if, for example: (a) the employee has accrued an excessive amount of paid annual leave; or (b) the employer’s enterprise is being shut down for a period (for example, between Christmas and New Year). Agreements about taking paid annual leave"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "bf0e5a5ce371e841d70f14c084431cec12933d96f3da54d29a32e362ea281d5d" ;
    values:partOf concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-94 ;
    cof:pageNumber "248"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Employer may require employee to take paid annual leave if reasonable." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <fair-work-act-2009.pdf> ;
    dc:source "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.248" ;
