concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-97 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "97 Taking paid personal/carer’s leave"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-97 ;
    values:originalText "An employee may take paid personal/carer’s leave if the leave is taken: (a) because the employee is not fit for work because of a personal illness, or personal injury, affecting the employee; or (b) to provide care or support to a member of the employee’s immediate family, or a member of the employee’s household, who requires care or support because of:  Terms and conditions of employment  Chapter 2 The National Employment Standards  Part 2-2 Personal/carer’s leave, compassionate leave and paid family and domestic violence leave  Division 7 Section 98 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 (i) a personal illness, or personal injury, affecting the member; or (ii) an unexpected emergency affecting the member. Note 1: The notice and evidence requirements of section 107 must be complied with. Note 2: If an employee has an entitlement to paid personal/carer’s leave, the employee may take that leave instead of taking unpaid special parental leave under section 80." ;
    skos:definition "An employee may take paid personal/carer’s leave if the leave is taken: (a) because the employee is not fit for work because of a personal illness, or personal injury, affecting the employee; or (b) to provide care or support to a member of the employee’s immediate family, or a member of the employee’s household, who requires care or support because of:  Terms and conditions of employment  Chapter 2 The National Employment Standards  Part 2-2 Personal/carer’s leave, compassionate leave and paid family and domestic violence leave  Division 7 Section 98 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 (i) a personal illness, or personal injury, affecting the member; or (ii) an unexpected emergency affecting the member. Note 1: The notice and evidence requirements of section 107 must be complied with. Note 2: If an employee has an entitlement to paid personal/carer’s leave, the employee may take that leave instead of taking unpaid special parental leave under section 80."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "3665335de6d03bf11465fdca4e8be6f23afd54cb0a682f9af5dff6a4c0bc1b79" ;
    cof:pageNumber "250"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "An employee may take paid personal/carer’s leave under certain conditions." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
