doc:sec-101-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "101(2) Modern awards and enterprise agreements may include terms" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) The terms must require that: (a) paid personal/carer’s leave must not be cashed out if the cashing out would result in the employee’s remaining accrued entitlement to paid personal/carer’s leave being less than 15 days; and (b) each cashing out of a particular amount of paid personal/carer’s leave must be by a separate agreement in writing between the employer and the employee; and (c) the employee must be paid at least the full amount that would have been payable to the employee had the employee taken the leave that the employee has forgone. Subdivision B—Unpaid carer’s leave" ;
    cof:pageNumber "252"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-102 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "102 Entitlement to unpaid carer’s leave"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-102 ;
    values:originalText "An employee is entitled to 2 days of unpaid carer’s leave for each occasion (a permissible occasion) when a member of the employee’s immediate family, or a member of the employee’s household, requires care or support because of: (a) a personal illness, or personal injury, affecting the member; or (b) an unexpected emergency affecting the member.  Terms and conditions of employment  Chapter 2 The National Employment Standards  Part 2-2 Personal/carer’s leave, compassionate leave and paid family and domestic violence leave  Division 7 Section 103 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026" ;
    skos:definition "An employee is entitled to 2 days of unpaid carer’s leave for each occasion (a permissible occasion) when a member of the employee’s immediate family, or a member of the employee’s household, requires care or support because of: (a) a personal illness, or personal injury, affecting the member; or (b) an unexpected emergency affecting the member.  Terms and conditions of employment  Chapter 2 The National Employment Standards  Part 2-2 Personal/carer’s leave, compassionate leave and paid family and domestic violence leave  Division 7 Section 103 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "e8be464547ecd3c7471a723c80a6cd30e1bb0eaec7dfed1049bc03c61c41dc87" ;
    cof:pageNumber "252"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Entitlement to unpaid carer’s leave for family members or household members requiring care due to illness, injury, or emergency." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <fair-work-act-2009.pdf> ;
    dc:source "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.252" ;
