    values:originalText "An employee is entitled to 2 days of unpaid carer’s leave for each occasion (a permissible occasion) when a member of the employee’s immediate family, or a member of the employee’s household, requires care or support because of: (a) a personal illness, or personal injury, affecting the member; or (b) an unexpected emergency affecting the member.  Terms and conditions of employment  Chapter 2 The National Employment Standards  Part 2-2 Personal/carer’s leave, compassionate leave and paid family and domestic violence leave  Division 7 Section 103 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026" ;
