doc:sec-105-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "105(2) Taking compassionate leave" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) An employee may take compassionate leave for a particular permissible occasion as: (a) a single continuous 2 day period; or (b) 2 separate periods of 1 day each; or (c) any separate periods to which the employee and his or her employer agree." ;
    cof:pageNumber "254"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-105-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "105(3) Taking compassionate leave"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-105-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) If the permissible occasion is the contraction or development of a personal illness, or the sustaining of a personal injury, the employee may take the compassionate leave for that occasion at any time while the illness or injury persists. Note: The notice and evidence requirements of section 107 must be complied with.  Terms and conditions of employment  Chapter 2 The National Employment Standards  Part 2-2 Personal/carer’s leave, compassionate leave and paid family and domestic violence leave  Division 7 Section 106 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026" ;
    skos:definition "(3) If the permissible occasion is the contraction or development of a personal illness, or the sustaining of a personal injury, the employee may take the compassionate leave for that occasion at any time while the illness or injury persists. Note: The notice and evidence requirements of section 107 must be complied with.  Terms and conditions of employment  Chapter 2 The National Employment Standards  Part 2-2 Personal/carer’s leave, compassionate leave and paid family and domestic violence leave  Division 7 Section 106 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "a4ff41cba9669839ae8d954cb41d47458deea79e987a50f3615bfcb95bed121e" ;
    values:partOf concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-105 ;
    cof:pageNumber "254"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Employee may take compassionate leave at any time while illness or injury persists." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
