doc:sec-106d-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "106D(2) Operation of paid family and domestic violence leave and" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) If an employee who is entitled, under a law of a State or Territory, to leave for victims of crime is also entitled to leave under this Subdivision, that law applies in addition to this Subdivision." ;
    cof:pageNumber "258"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-106d-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "106D(3) Operation of paid family and domestic violence leave and"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-106d-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) A person who is a national system employee only because of section 30C or 30M is entitled to leave under this Subdivision only to the extent that the leave would not constitute leave for victims of crime. Note: To the extent that leave would constitute leave for victims of crime, the entitlement to paid family and domestic violence leave is extended to the persons mentioned in subsection (3) by Division 2A of Part 6-3 (see subsection 757B(2))." ;
    skos:definition "(3) A person who is a national system employee only because of section 30C or 30M is entitled to leave under this Subdivision only to the extent that the leave would not constitute leave for victims of crime. Note: To the extent that leave would constitute leave for victims of crime, the entitlement to paid family and domestic violence leave is extended to the persons mentioned in subsection (3) by Division 2A of Part 6-3 (see subsection 757B(2))."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "3a1853a5c3e7e618cf627f1acc4e4c8db051590f26ff9f1b0c88e2905d501d18" ;
    values:partOf concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-106d ;
    cof:pageNumber "258"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "A national system employee is entitled to leave under this Subdivision only to the extent that the leave would not constitute leave for victims of crime." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
