    cof:title "115(1) Meaning of public holiday" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) The following are public holidays: (a) each of these days: (i) 1 January (New Year’s Day); (ii) 26 January (Australia Day); (iii) Good Friday; (iv) Easter Monday; (v) 25 April (Anzac Day); (vi) the holiday for the birthday of the Sovereign (on the day on which it is celebrated in a State or Territory or a region of a State or Territory); (vii) 25 December (Christmas Day); (viii) 26 December (Boxing Day); (b) any other day, or part-day, declared or prescribed by or under a law of a State or Territory to be observed generally within the State or Territory, or a region of the State or Territory, as a public holiday, other than a day or part-day, or a kind of day or part-day, that is excluded by the regulations from counting as a public holiday. Substituted public holidays under State or Territory laws" ;
    cof:pageNumber "272"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-115-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "115(2) Meaning of public holiday"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-115-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) If, under (or in accordance with a procedure under) a law of a State or Territory, a day or part-day is substituted for a day or part-day that would otherwise be a public holiday because of subsection (1), then the substituted day or part-day is the public holiday.  Terms and conditions of employment  Chapter 2 The National Employment Standards  Part 2-2 Public holidays  Division 10 Section 116 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 Substituted public holidays under modern awards and enterprise agreements" ;
    skos:definition "(2) If, under (or in accordance with a procedure under) a law of a State or Territory, a day or part-day is substituted for a day or part-day that would otherwise be a public holiday because of subsection (1), then the substituted day or part-day is the public holiday.  Terms and conditions of employment  Chapter 2 The National Employment Standards  Part 2-2 Public holidays  Division 10 Section 116 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 Substituted public holidays under modern awards and enterprise agreements"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "6ce28298bd4e4265d11ef03257db047cd5f21d93bcff4f5558b265bd23120287" ;
    values:partOf concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-115 ;
    cof:pageNumber "272"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Substituted day or part-day is the public holiday." ;
