    values:originalText "If, in accordance with this Division, an employee is absent from his or her employment on a day or part-day that is a public holiday, the employer must pay the employee at the employee’s base rate of pay for the employee’s ordinary hours of work on the day or part-day. Note: If the employee does not have ordinary hours of work on the public holiday, the employee is not entitled to payment under this section. For example, the employee is not entitled to payment if the employee is a casual employee who is not rostered on for the public holiday, or is a part-time employee whose part-time hours do not include the day of the week on which the public holiday occurs.  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment" ;
    cof:pageNumber "273"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-116a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "116A Division does not apply to certain employees or employers in"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-116a ;
    values:originalText "referring States This Division does not apply in relation to: (a) an employee who is a national system employee only because of section 30C or 30M (which extend the meaning of national system employee); or (b) an employer that is a national system employer only because of section 30D or 30N (which extend the meaning of national system employer)." ;
    skos:definition "referring States This Division does not apply in relation to: (a) an employee who is a national system employee only because of section 30C or 30M (which extend the meaning of national system employee); or (b) an employer that is a national system employer only because of section 30D or 30N (which extend the meaning of national system employer)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "78383cb7bb88bbf0ba7b3142a067d5e3b901286826ba79ee2f5c1878d44a77a9" ;
    cof:pageNumber "274"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Division does not apply to certain employees or employers." ;
