doc:sec-116b a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "116B Employer’s obligation to make superannuation contributions" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "An employer must make contributions to a superannuation fund for the benefit of an employee so as to avoid liability to pay superannuation guarantee charge under the Superannuation Guarantee Charge Act 1992 in relation to the employee." ;
    cof:pageNumber "274"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-116c a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "116C Reduction of employer’s liability to the extent of"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-116c ;
    values:originalText "superannuation charge payments The obligation to make contributions for an employee under section 116B does not apply to an employer to the extent that: (a) the employer has made a charge payment (within the meaning of section 63A of the Superannuation Guarantee (Administration) Act 1992) in respect of the employee under Part 8 of that Act; and (b) the employee is a benefiting employee (within the meaning of that Part); and (c) the Commissioner of Taxation is required to pay, or otherwise deal with, a shortfall component (within the meaning of that Part) for the benefit of the employee under that Part.  Terms and conditions of employment  Chapter 2 The National Employment Standards  Part 2-2 Superannuation contributions  Division 10A Section 116D Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026" ;
    skos:definition "superannuation charge payments The obligation to make contributions for an employee under section 116B does not apply to an employer to the extent that: (a) the employer has made a charge payment (within the meaning of section 63A of the Superannuation Guarantee (Administration) Act 1992) in respect of the employee under Part 8 of that Act; and (b) the employee is a benefiting employee (within the meaning of that Part); and (c) the Commissioner of Taxation is required to pay, or otherwise deal with, a shortfall component (within the meaning of that Part) for the benefit of the employee under that Part.  Terms and conditions of employment  Chapter 2 The National Employment Standards  Part 2-2 Superannuation contributions  Division 10A Section 116D Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "81b409aed09e5ae740da9ac59a0b46d19b820a8e60afd76b485a5d894b2a74eb" ;
    cof:pageNumber "274"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Reduction of employer's liability for superannuation charge payments" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <fair-work-act-2009.pdf> ;
    dc:source "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.274" ;
    cml:asserts concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-116c-norm .
