 day before the employer became bankrupt or went into liquidation—on or after the day that is 6 months before the insolvency practitioner was appointed; or (iii) if, before the last insolvency practitioner was appointed, other insolvency practitioners for the employer were appointed without any intervening business days between any of those appointments—on or after the day that is 6 months before the first of those insolvency practitioners was appointed; or (iv) due to the insolvency of the employer. (5) A members’ voluntary winding up is a winding up under section 495 of the Corporations Act 2001. Time of liquidation—members’ voluntary winding up where company turns out to be insolvent (6) If a liquidator takes action under section 496 of the Corporations Act 2001 (company turns out to be insolvent) in relation to a small business employer whose liquidation began as a members’  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment" ;
    cof:pageNumber "280"^^xsd:integer .

