doc:sec-156g-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "156G(2) Review of the default fund term of modern awards" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) The FWC must ensure that the following persons have a reasonable opportunity to make written submissions (including submissions requesting that a particular superannuation fund be specified in the term in relation to a standard MySuper product) to the FWC in relation to the default fund term of the award: (a) an employee and employer that are covered by the modern award; (b) an organisation that is entitled to represent the industrial interests of one or more employees or employers that are covered by the award; (c) if the award includes an outworker term—an organisation that is entitled to represent the industrial interests of one or more outworkers to whom the outworker term relates." ;
    cof:pageNumber "322"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-156g-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "156G(3) Review of the default fund term of modern awards"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-156g-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) If: (a) a person or body (whether or not a person referred to in subsection (2)) makes a written submission in relation to the default fund term of a modern award; and  Terms and conditions of employment  Chapter 2 Modern awards  Part 2-3 4 yearly reviews of default fund terms of modern awards  Division 4A Section 156H Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 (b) the person or body refers to a particular superannuation fund in the submission; and (c) the person or body has an interest in relation to that superannuation fund; then the person or body must disclose that interest in the submission." ;
    skos:definition "(3) If: (a) a person or body (whether or not a person referred to in subsection (2)) makes a written submission in relation to the default fund term of a modern award; and  Terms and conditions of employment  Chapter 2 Modern awards  Part 2-3 4 yearly reviews of default fund terms of modern awards  Division 4A Section 156H Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 (b) the person or body refers to a particular superannuation fund in the submission; and (c) the person or body has an interest in relation to that superannuation fund; then the person or body must disclose that interest in the submission."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "4146cdd052abb653b1e6d4a9d9980306ce208eefb98307dd44f4eebc8d50d8aa" ;
    values:partOf concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-156g ;
    cof:pageNumber "322"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Must disclose interest in superannuation fund if making a written submission." ;
    dc:description "Interest in relation to the superannuation fund mentioned in the submission." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
