doc:sec-156q a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "156Q The first stage test" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "An employer MySuper product satisfies the first stage test if the FWC is satisfied that including the product on the Schedule of Approved Employer MySuper Products would be in the best interests of default fund employees, or a particular class of those employees, taking into account: (a) the information provided in the application; and (b) the first stage criteria; and (c) any submissions that were made in relation to whether the product satisfies the first stage test." ;
    cof:pageNumber "327"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-156r a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "156R Submissions about the first stage test"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-156r ;
    values:originalText "(1) The FWC must ensure that all persons and bodies have a reasonable opportunity to make written submissions to the FWC about whether an employer MySuper product satisfies the first stage test. (2) If: (a) a person or body makes a written submission in relation to whether an employer MySuper product satisfies the first stage test; and (b) the person or body has an interest in relation to: (i) the superannuation fund that offers the product; or (ii) if the person or body refers to another superannuation fund in the submission—that superannuation fund; then the person or body must disclose that interest in the submission. (3) The FWC must publish any submission that is made.  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The FWC must ensure that all persons and bodies have a reasonable opportunity to make written submissions to the FWC about whether an employer MySuper product satisfies the first stage test. (2) If: (a) a person or body makes a written submission in relation to whether an employer MySuper product satisfies the first stage test; and (b) the person or body has an interest in relation to: (i) the superannuation fund that offers the product; or (ii) if the person or body refers to another superannuation fund in the submission—that superannuation fund; then the person or body must disclose that interest in the submission. (3) The FWC must publish any submission that is made.  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "edb699a681c9ae9c066ebf84048f6d4b8bd3d756decb54e41c8896ac137a746a" ;
    cof:pageNumber "327"^^xsd:integer ;
