doc:sec-164-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "164(1) Special criteria for revoking modern awards" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) A determination under this Part that varies a modern award (other than a determination that sets, varies or revokes modern award minimum wages) comes into operation on the day specified in the determination. Note 1: For when a modern award, or a revocation of a modern award, comes into operation, see section 49. Note: For when a determination under this Part setting, varying or revoking modern award minimum wages comes into operation, see section 166.  Terms and conditions of employment  Chapter 2 Modern awards  Part 2-3 General provisions relating to modern award powers  Division 6 Section 166 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026" ;
    cof:pageNumber "338"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-164-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "164(2) Special criteria for revoking modern awards"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-164-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) The specified day must not be earlier than the day on which the determination is made, unless: (a) the determination is made under section 160 (which deals with variation to remove ambiguities or correct errors); and (b) the FWC is satisfied that there are exceptional circumstances that justify specifying an earlier day. Determinations take effect from first full pay period" ;
    skos:definition "(2) The specified day must not be earlier than the day on which the determination is made, unless: (a) the determination is made under section 160 (which deals with variation to remove ambiguities or correct errors); and (b) the FWC is satisfied that there are exceptional circumstances that justify specifying an earlier day. Determinations take effect from first full pay period"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ab804362fbc4bb5ae0dfd84bfa409a9639e046f643a3886f12fb5b582bc43789" ;
    values:partOf concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-164 ;
    cof:pageNumber "338"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "The FWC must not specify another day unless it is satisfied that it is appropriate to do so. Determination must not be made earlier than specified day unless exceptional circumstances justify." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
