doc:sec-164-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "164(2) Special criteria for revoking modern awards" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) The specified day must not be earlier than the day on which the determination is made, unless: (a) the determination is made under section 160 (which deals with variation to remove ambiguities or correct errors); and (b) the FWC is satisfied that there are exceptional circumstances that justify specifying an earlier day. Determinations take effect from first full pay period" ;
    cof:pageNumber "338"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-164-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "164(3) Special criteria for revoking modern awards"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-164-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) The determination does not take effect in relation to a particular employee until the start of the employee’s first full pay period that starts on or after the day the determination comes into operation. 166  When variation determinations setting, varying or revoking modern award minimum wages come into operation Determinations generally come into operation on 1 July" ;
    skos:definition "(3) The determination does not take effect in relation to a particular employee until the start of the employee’s first full pay period that starts on or after the day the determination comes into operation. 166  When variation determinations setting, varying or revoking modern award minimum wages come into operation Determinations generally come into operation on 1 July"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "cadf7e37e126a8a525131610a7fbc236979edd52c2f6603c93780f5b8e4788da" ;
    values:partOf concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-164 ;
    cof:pageNumber "338"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "The specified day must not be earlier than the day on which the determination is made. Employee's first full pay period must start on or after the day of determination operation." ;
