doc:sec-167-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "167(2) Special rules relating to retrospective variations of awards" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) If, before the determination was made, an enterprise agreement or a variation of an enterprise agreement was approved by the FWC, the validity of the approval is not affected by the retrospective effect of the determination.  Terms and conditions of employment  Chapter 2 Modern awards  Part 2-3 General provisions relating to modern award powers  Division 6 Section 168 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 No creation of liability to pay pecuniary penalty for past conduct" ;
    cof:pageNumber "340"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-167-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "167(3) Special rules relating to retrospective variations of awards"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-167-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) If: (a) a person engaged in conduct before the determination was made; and (b) but for the retrospective effect of the determination, the conduct would not have contravened a term of the modern award or an enterprise agreement; a court must not order the person to pay a pecuniary penalty under Division 2 of Part 4-1 in relation to the conduct, on the grounds that the conduct contravened a term of the modern award or enterprise agreement. Note 1: This subsection does not affect the powers of a court to make other kinds of orders under Division 2 of Part 4-1. Note 2: A determination varying a modern award could result in a contravention of a term of an enterprise agreement because of the effect of subsection 206(2)." ;
    skos:definition "(3) If: (a) a person engaged in conduct before the determination was made; and (b) but for the retrospective effect of the determination, the conduct would not have contravened a term of the modern award or an enterprise agreement; a court must not order the person to pay a pecuniary penalty under Division 2 of Part 4-1 in relation to the conduct, on the grounds that the conduct contravened a term of the modern award or enterprise agreement. Note 1: This subsection does not affect the powers of a court to make other kinds of orders under Division 2 of Part 4-1. Note 2: A determination varying a modern award could result in a contravention of a term of an enterprise agreement because of the effect of subsection 206(2)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "55ae11380dd9a3589c6e94c8dae91d312b3d9ef6482f4f6cafd5b44173bc7f8f" ;
    values:partOf concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-167 ;
    cof:pageNumber "340"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "No pecuniary penalty for conduct before determination if it wouldn't have contravened a term of the modern award or enterprise agreement." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <fair-work-act-2009.pdf> ;
    dc:source "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.340" ;
