concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-178b a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "178B Notified negotiation period for a proposed single-enterprise"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-178b ;
    values:originalText "agreement that is a greenfields agreement (1) If a proposed single-enterprise agreement is a greenfields agreement, an employer that is a bargaining representative for the agreement may give written notice: (a) to each employee organisation that is a bargaining representative for the agreement; and (b) stating that the period of 6 months beginning on a specified day is the notified negotiation period for the agreement. (2) The specified day must be later than:  Terms and conditions of employment  Chapter 2 Enterprise agreements  Part 2-4 Bargaining and representation during bargaining  Division 3 Section 178B Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 (a) if only one employee organisation is a bargaining representative for the agreement—the day on which the employer gave the notice to the organisation; or (b) if 2 or more employee organisations are bargaining representatives for the agreement—the last day on which the employer gave the notice to any of those organisations. Multiple employers—agreement to giving of notice (3) If 2 or more employers are bargaining representatives for the agreement, the notice has no effect unless the other employer or employers agree to the giving of the notice.  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment" ;
    skos:definition "agreement that is a greenfields agreement (1) If a proposed single-enterprise agreement is a greenfields agreement, an employer that is a bargaining representative for the agreement may give written notice: (a) to each employee organisation that is a bargaining representative for the agreement; and (b) stating that the period of 6 months beginning on a specified day is the notified negotiation period for the agreement. (2) The specified day must be later than:  Terms and conditions of employment  Chapter 2 Enterprise agreements  Part 2-4 Bargaining and representation during bargaining  Division 3 Section 178B Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 (a) if only one employee organisation is a bargaining representative for the agreement—the day on which the employer gave the notice to the organisation; or (b) if 2 or more employee organisations are bargaining representatives for the agreement—the last day on which the employer gave the notice to any of those organisations. Multiple employers—agreement to giving of notice (3) If 2 or more employers are bargaining representatives for the agreement, the notice has no effect unless the other employer or employers agree to the giving of the notice.  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "8103645bbc96146389eb699e51f0420a0a6e4eae006195aa319e9054389e7d24" ;
    cof:pageNumber "368"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-178b-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-178b-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-178b-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
