doc:sec-188-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "188(1) Determining whether an enterprise agreement has been" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) The FWC must take into account the statement of principles made under section 188B in determining whether it is satisfied that an enterprise agreement has been genuinely agreed to by the employees covered by the agreement. Sufficient interest and sufficiently representative" ;
    cof:pageNumber "384"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-188-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "188(2) Determining whether an enterprise agreement has been"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-188-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) The FWC cannot be satisfied that an enterprise agreement has been genuinely agreed to by the employees covered by the agreement unless the FWC is satisfied that the employees requested to approve the agreement by voting for it: (a) have a sufficient interest in the terms of the agreement; and  Terms and conditions of employment  Chapter 2 Enterprise agreements  Part 2-4 Approval of enterprise agreements  Division 4 Section 188 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 (b) are sufficiently representative, having regard to the employees the agreement is expressed to cover. Note: In One Key Workforce Pty Ltd v Construction, Forestry, Mining and Energy Union [2018] FCAFC 77 (2018) 262 FCR 527, a Full Court of the Federal Court observed that whether an agreement has been genuinely agreed involves consideration of the authenticity of the agreement of the employees, including whether the employees who voted for the agreement had an informed and genuine understanding of what was being approved. Agreement of bargaining representatives that are employee organisations" ;
    skos:definition "(2) The FWC cannot be satisfied that an enterprise agreement has been genuinely agreed to by the employees covered by the agreement unless the FWC is satisfied that the employees requested to approve the agreement by voting for it: (a) have a sufficient interest in the terms of the agreement; and  Terms and conditions of employment  Chapter 2 Enterprise agreements  Part 2-4 Approval of enterprise agreements  Division 4 Section 188 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 (b) are sufficiently representative, having regard to the employees the agreement is expressed to cover. Note: In One Key Workforce Pty Ltd v Construction, Forestry, Mining and Energy Union [2018] FCAFC 77 (2018) 262 FCR 527, a Full Court of the Federal Court observed that whether an agreement has been genuinely agreed involves consideration of the authenticity of the agreement of the employees, including whether the employees who voted for the agreement had an informed and genuine understanding of what was being approved. Agreement of bargaining representatives that are employee organisations"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ea1fc6b7fd215c23a5589dbfb2a06f4d537caea25367fabd1d52bdc363b97474" ;
