doc:sec-193a-ss-6 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "193A(6) Applying the better off overall test" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(6) The FWC may only have regard to patterns or kinds of work, or types of employment, if they are reasonably foreseeable at the test time. In considering what is reasonably foreseeable, the FWC must have regard to the nature of the enterprise or enterprises to which the agreement relates." ;
    cof:pageNumber "394"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-193a-ss-6a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "193A(6A) Applying the better off overall test"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-193a-ss-6a ;
    values:originalText "(6A) The FWC must determine whether a particular pattern or kind of work, or type of employment, is reasonably foreseeable for the purposes of subsection (6) if a view is expressed by any of the following that it is, or is not, reasonably foreseeable: (a) the employer or employers that are covered by the agreement;  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment" ;
    skos:definition "(6A) The FWC must determine whether a particular pattern or kind of work, or type of employment, is reasonably foreseeable for the purposes of subsection (6) if a view is expressed by any of the following that it is, or is not, reasonably foreseeable: (a) the employer or employers that are covered by the agreement;  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "0111d13bb93878b47b22bbbc0bc341f93f06d7ade75384b17c58d46ae1af5036" ;
    values:partOf concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-193a ;
    cof:pageNumber "394"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Employer must determine foreseeability of work type or employment" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
