concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-197 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "197 Pieceworkers—enterprise agreement includes pieceworker term"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-197 ;
    values:originalText "Application of this section (1) This section applies if: (a) an enterprise agreement that covers an employee includes a term that defines or describes the employee as a pieceworker; and (b) a modern award that is in operation and covers the employee does not include such a term. No detriment test (2) The FWC must be satisfied that the effect of including such a term in the agreement is not detrimental to the employee in relation to  Terms and conditions of employment  Chapter 2 Enterprise agreements  Part 2-4 Approval of enterprise agreements  Division 4 Section 198 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 the entitlements of the employee under the National Employment Standards." ;
    skos:definition "Application of this section (1) This section applies if: (a) an enterprise agreement that covers an employee includes a term that defines or describes the employee as a pieceworker; and (b) a modern award that is in operation and covers the employee does not include such a term. No detriment test (2) The FWC must be satisfied that the effect of including such a term in the agreement is not detrimental to the employee in relation to  Terms and conditions of employment  Chapter 2 Enterprise agreements  Part 2-4 Approval of enterprise agreements  Division 4 Section 198 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 the entitlements of the employee under the National Employment Standards."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "0ccdf42586937399ceba0f448d92994a11335c8f0a2c4f649309a780bb974a92" ;
    cof:pageNumber "402"^^xsd:integer ;
