concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-217a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "217A FWC may deal with certain disputes about variations"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-217a ;
    values:originalText "(1) This section applies if a variation of an enterprise agreement is proposed. (2) An employer or employee organisation covered by the enterprise agreement or an affected employee for the variation may apply to the FWC for the FWC to deal with a dispute about the proposed variation if the employer and the affected employees are unable to resolve the dispute. (3) The FWC must not arbitrate (however described) the dispute.  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment" ;
    skos:definition "(1) This section applies if a variation of an enterprise agreement is proposed. (2) An employer or employee organisation covered by the enterprise agreement or an affected employee for the variation may apply to the FWC for the FWC to deal with a dispute about the proposed variation if the employer and the affected employees are unable to resolve the dispute. (3) The FWC must not arbitrate (however described) the dispute.  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "a15bc510599366072866593ade49890a9b6a1f3ef4ccd2ff5d5e1c6db777f37e" ;
    cof:pageNumber "451"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-217a-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-217a-ss-2 ;
