    cof:title "220(2) Employers may request employees to approve a proposed" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) Before making the request, the employer must: (a) take all reasonable steps to notify the employees of the following: (i) the time and place at which the vote will occur; (ii) the voting method that will be used; and (b) give the employees a reasonable opportunity to decide whether they want to approve the proposed termination." ;
    cof:pageNumber "454"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-220-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "220(3) Employers may request employees to approve a proposed"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-220-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) Without limiting subsection (1), the employer may request that the employees vote by ballot or by an electronic method. 221  When termination of an enterprise agreement is agreed to Single-enterprise agreement" ;
    skos:definition "(3) Without limiting subsection (1), the employer may request that the employees vote by ballot or by an electronic method. 221  When termination of an enterprise agreement is agreed to Single-enterprise agreement"@en ;
