concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-220-ss-1 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "220(1) Employers may request employees to approve a proposed"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-220-ss-1 ;
    values:originalText "(1) If the employees of an employer, or each employer, covered by a single-enterprise agreement have been asked to approve a proposed termination of the agreement under subsection 220(1), the termination is agreed to when a majority of the employees who cast a valid vote approve the termination.  Terms and conditions of employment  Chapter 2 Enterprise agreements  Part 2-4 Variation and termination of enterprise agreements  Division 7 Section 222 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 Multi-enterprise agreement" ;
    skos:definition "(1) If the employees of an employer, or each employer, covered by a single-enterprise agreement have been asked to approve a proposed termination of the agreement under subsection 220(1), the termination is agreed to when a majority of the employees who cast a valid vote approve the termination.  Terms and conditions of employment  Chapter 2 Enterprise agreements  Part 2-4 Variation and termination of enterprise agreements  Division 7 Section 222 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 Multi-enterprise agreement"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "f4a8526fee479221b920f307db833c6f2003f648d50144340261bbb08cc33eed" ;
    values:partOf concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-220 ;
    cof:pageNumber "454"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Majority approval required for termination of enterprise agreement Employers must request employee approval for proposed termination of an enterprise agreement." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <fair-work-act-2009.pdf> ;
