doc:sec-226a-ss-4 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "226A(4) Guarantee of termination entitlements" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(4) A guarantee of termination entitlements given in relation to the termination of an enterprise agreement: (a) comes into force on the day on which the termination of the agreement comes into operation under section 227; and  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment" ;
    cof:pageNumber "458"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-227a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "227A Application for FWC to reconsider whether an enterprise"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-227a ;
    values:originalText "agreement passes the better off overall test (1) If the condition in subsection (2) is satisfied, any of the following may apply to the FWC for a reconsideration of whether an enterprise agreement passes the better off overall test: (a) one or more of the employers covered by the agreement; (b) an employee covered by the agreement; (c) an employee organisation covered by the agreement. (2) The condition in this subsection is satisfied if: (a) before approving the agreement the FWC had regard, under subsection 193A(6), to patterns or kinds of work, or types of employment engaged in, or to be engaged in, by: (i) the award covered employees for the agreement; and (ii) if the agreement is a single-enterprise agreement that covers one or more employees to whom a supported bargaining agreement or a single interest employer agreement applies—those employees; and (b) at the test time or a later time, one or more employees covered by subsection (4) or (5) engaged in other patterns or kinds of work, or other types of employment, to which the FWC did not have regard under subsection 193A(6). Example: Before approving the agreement the FWC had regard, under subsection 193A(6), to work on Saturdays and Sundays as a pattern of work for a class of employees. At the test time some employees covered by subsection (4) worked only on Sundays, and the FWC did not have regard, under subsection 193A(6), to this pattern of work. In these circumstances, the condition in this subsection is satisfied. (4) An employee is covered by this subsection if, on the assumption that the test time mentioned in paragraph 193(4)(b) were the time  Terms and conditions of employment  Chapter 2 Enterprise agreements  Part 2-4 Reconsideration of whether an enterprise agreement passes the better off overall test" ;
    skos:definition "agreement passes the better off overall test (1) If the condition in subsection (2) is satisfied, any of the following may apply to the FWC for a reconsideration of whether an enterprise agreement passes the better off overall test: (a) one or more of the employers covered by the agreement; (b) an employee covered by the agreement; (c) an employee organisation covered by the agreement. (2) The condition in this subsection is satisfied if: (a) before approving the agreement the FWC had regard, under subsection 193A(6), to patterns or kinds of work, or types of employment engaged in, or to be engaged in, by: (i) the award covered employees for the agreement; and (ii) if the agreement is a single-enterprise agreement that covers one or more employees to whom a supported bargaining agreement or a single interest employer agreement applies—those employees; and (b) at the test time or a later time, one or more employees covered by subsection (4) or (5) engaged in other patterns or kinds of work, or other types of employment, to which the FWC did not have regard under subsection 193A(6). Example: Before approving the agreement the FWC had regard, under subsection 193A(6), to work on Saturdays and Sundays as a pattern of work for a class of employees. At the test time some employees covered by subsection (4) worked only on Sundays, and the FWC did not have regard, under subsection 193A(6), to this pattern of work. In these circumstances, the condition in this subsection is satisfied. (4) An employee is covered by this subsection if, on the assumption that the test time mentioned in paragraph 193(4)(b) were the time  Terms and conditions of employment  Chapter 2 Enterprise agreements  Part 2-4 Reconsideration of whether an enterprise agreement passes the better off overall test"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "f5b8b6ec5c78ba11f6f308897148ee30caafe5c5407caff67383f848bad48899" ;
    cof:pageNumber "462"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-227a-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-227a-ss-2 ;
