concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-229-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "229(4) Applications for bargaining orders"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-229-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) The bargaining representative may only apply for the bargaining order if the bargaining representative: (a) has concerns that: (i) one or more of the bargaining representatives for the agreement have not met, or are not meeting, the good faith bargaining requirements; or (ii) the bargaining process is not proceeding efficiently or fairly because there are multiple bargaining representatives for the agreement; and (b) has given a written notice setting out those concerns to the relevant bargaining representatives; and (c) has given the relevant bargaining representatives a reasonable time within which to respond to those concerns; and (d) considers that the relevant bargaining representatives have not responded appropriately to those concerns. Non-compliance with notice requirements may be permitted" ;
    skos:definition "(4) The bargaining representative may only apply for the bargaining order if the bargaining representative: (a) has concerns that: (i) one or more of the bargaining representatives for the agreement have not met, or are not meeting, the good faith bargaining requirements; or (ii) the bargaining process is not proceeding efficiently or fairly because there are multiple bargaining representatives for the agreement; and (b) has given a written notice setting out those concerns to the relevant bargaining representatives; and (c) has given the relevant bargaining representatives a reasonable time within which to respond to those concerns; and (d) considers that the relevant bargaining representatives have not responded appropriately to those concerns. Non-compliance with notice requirements may be permitted"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "2b2a2d0f8f4280d11fd0f45970e14861b864109dc9695ff3d9c903bc822060f3" ;
    values:partOf concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-229 ;
    cof:pageNumber "468"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Bargaining representative must apply for bargaining order under certain conditions." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <fair-work-act-2009.pdf> ;
