doc:sec-234-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "234(2) Applications for intractable bargaining declarations" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) The FWC must be satisfied that: (a) the FWC has dealt with the dispute about the agreement under section 240 and the applicant participated in the FWC’s processes to deal with the dispute; and  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment" ;
    cof:pageNumber "473"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-235a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "235A Post-declaration negotiating period"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-235a ;
    values:originalText "(1) The FWC may, if it considers it appropriate to do so, specify in the declaration a period (the post-declaration negotiating period) that: (a) starts on the day the declaration is made; and (b) ends on: (i) the day specified by the FWC in the declaration; or (ii) any later day determined under subsection (2). Note: The FWC cannot make an intractable bargaining workplace determination during any post-declaration negotiating period (see section 269) but may still provide other assistance during the period, such as conciliation. (2) The FWC may, if it considers it appropriate to do so and taking into account any views of the bargaining representatives, extend the period referred to in subsection (1) by determining a later day for the purposes of subparagraph (1)(b)(ii).  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The FWC may, if it considers it appropriate to do so, specify in the declaration a period (the post-declaration negotiating period) that: (a) starts on the day the declaration is made; and (b) ends on: (i) the day specified by the FWC in the declaration; or (ii) any later day determined under subsection (2). Note: The FWC cannot make an intractable bargaining workplace determination during any post-declaration negotiating period (see section 269) but may still provide other assistance during the period, such as conciliation. (2) The FWC may, if it considers it appropriate to do so and taking into account any views of the bargaining representatives, extend the period referred to in subsection (1) by determining a later day for the purposes of subparagraph (1)(b)(ii).  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "98b2eae7cec6ef6c6ab799d944ba996f3d314675b69ba8d80a5c1e7993880fc9" ;
    cof:pageNumber "475"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-235a-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-235a-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <fair-work-act-2009.pdf> ;
    dc:source "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.475" .
doc:sec-235a a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "235A Post-declaration negotiating period" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) The FWC may, if it considers it appropriate to do so, specify in the declaration a period (the post-declaration negotiating period) that: (a) starts on the day the declaration is made; and (b) ends on: (i) the day specified by the FWC in the declaration; or (ii) any later day determined under subsection (2). Note: The FWC cannot make an intractable bargaining workplace determination during any post-declaration negotiating period (see section 269) but may still provide other assistance during the period, such as conciliation. (2) The FWC may, if it considers it appropriate to do so and taking into account any views of the bargaining representatives, extend the period referred to in subsection (1) by determining a later day for the purposes of subparagraph (1)(b)(ii).  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment" ;
    cof:pageNumber "475"^^xsd:integer .

