concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-238-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "238(4) Scope orders"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-238-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) The FWC may make the scope order if the FWC is satisfied: (a) that the bargaining representative who made the application has met, or is meeting, the good faith bargaining requirements; and (b) that making the order will promote the fair and efficient conduct of bargaining; and (c) that the group of employees who will be covered by the agreement proposed to be specified in the scope order was fairly chosen; and (d) it is reasonable in all the circumstances to make the order. Matters which the FWC must take into account" ;
    skos:definition "(4) The FWC may make the scope order if the FWC is satisfied: (a) that the bargaining representative who made the application has met, or is meeting, the good faith bargaining requirements; and (b) that making the order will promote the fair and efficient conduct of bargaining; and (c) that the group of employees who will be covered by the agreement proposed to be specified in the scope order was fairly chosen; and (d) it is reasonable in all the circumstances to make the order. Matters which the FWC must take into account"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "27624a319ded39b01be12606b3a94b1420872dae1e9e419dae886e8cc6e0d8d8" ;
    values:partOf concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-238 ;
