    cof:title "242(1) Supported bargaining authorisations" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) The FWC must make a supported bargaining authorisation in relation to a proposed multi-enterprise agreement if: (a) an application for the authorisation has been made; and (b) the FWC is satisfied that it is appropriate for the employers and employees (which may be some or all of the employers or employees specified in the application) that will be covered by the agreement to bargain together, having regard to: (i) the prevailing pay and conditions within the relevant industry or sector (including whether low rates of pay prevail in the industry or sector); and (ii) whether the employers have clearly identifiable common interests; and (iii) whether the likely number of bargaining representatives for the agreement would be consistent with a manageable collective bargaining process; and (iv) any other matters the FWC considers appropriate; and (c) the FWC is satisfied that at least some of the employees who will be covered by the agreement are represented by an employee organisation. Note: This subsection is subject to section 243A (restrictions on making supported bargaining authorisations). Common interests" ;
    cof:pageNumber "484"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-242-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "242(2) Supported bargaining authorisations"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-242-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) For the purposes of subparagraph (1)(b)(ii), examples of common interests that employers may have include the following: (a) a geographical location; (b) the nature of the enterprises to which the agreement will relate, and the terms and conditions of employment in those enterprises;  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment" ;
    skos:definition "(2) For the purposes of subparagraph (1)(b)(ii), examples of common interests that employers may have include the following: (a) a geographical location; (b) the nature of the enterprises to which the agreement will relate, and the terms and conditions of employment in those enterprises;  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b7fe4af868794f7f4a7f94cce98795f55d7a1fb6e222ce8cfff77d715ff26f87" ;
    values:partOf concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-242 ;
    cof:pageNumber "484"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Employers and employees must be specified in the agreement. Examples of common interests that employers may have" ;
    dc:description "Yes" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
