concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-244 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "244 Variation of supported bargaining authorisations—general"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-244 ;
    values:originalText "Variation to remove employer (1) An employer specified in a supported bargaining authorisation may apply to the FWC for a variation of the authorisation to remove the employer’s name from the authorisation. (2) If an application is made under subsection (1), the FWC must vary the authorisation to remove the employer’s name if the FWC is satisfied that, because of a change in the employer’s circumstances, it is no longer appropriate for the employer to be specified in the authorisation.  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment" ;
    skos:definition "Variation to remove employer (1) An employer specified in a supported bargaining authorisation may apply to the FWC for a variation of the authorisation to remove the employer’s name from the authorisation. (2) If an application is made under subsection (1), the FWC must vary the authorisation to remove the employer’s name if the FWC is satisfied that, because of a change in the employer’s circumstances, it is no longer appropriate for the employer to be specified in the authorisation.  Chapter 2  Terms and conditions of employment"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "02cdf4d90012928d2c63a341dcd191b8b446cb120c477306c0090904dba35f66" ;
    cof:pageNumber "487"^^xsd:integer ;
