concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-245 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "245 Variation of supported bargaining authorisations—enterprise"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-245 ;
    values:originalText "agreement etc. comes into operation (1) The FWC is taken to have varied a supported bargaining authorisation to remove an employer’s name when the employer and all of their employees who are specified in the authorisation are covered by an enterprise agreement, or a workplace determination, that is in operation. (2) The FWC is taken to have varied a supported bargaining authorisation to remove an employee when the employee is covered by an enterprise agreement, or a workplace determination, that is in operation." ;
    skos:definition "agreement etc. comes into operation (1) The FWC is taken to have varied a supported bargaining authorisation to remove an employer’s name when the employer and all of their employees who are specified in the authorisation are covered by an enterprise agreement, or a workplace determination, that is in operation. (2) The FWC is taken to have varied a supported bargaining authorisation to remove an employee when the employee is covered by an enterprise agreement, or a workplace determination, that is in operation."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "d036b5f9d5ad0e1513aa7f4fb05665ff4fc6743ddc519c4044eff3f70ef4188b" ;
    cof:pageNumber "489"^^xsd:integer ;
