    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-246-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) The FWC may, on its own initiative, provide to the bargaining representatives for the agreement such assistance: (a) that the FWC considers appropriate to facilitate bargaining for the agreement; and (b) that the FWC could provide if it were dealing with a dispute. Note: This section does not empower the FWC to arbitrate, because subsection 595(3) provides that the FWC may arbitrate only if expressly authorised to do so. FWC may direct a person to attend a conference" ;
    skos:definition "(2) The FWC may, on its own initiative, provide to the bargaining representatives for the agreement such assistance: (a) that the FWC considers appropriate to facilitate bargaining for the agreement; and (b) that the FWC could provide if it were dealing with a dispute. Note: This section does not empower the FWC to arbitrate, because subsection 595(3) provides that the FWC may arbitrate only if expressly authorised to do so. FWC may direct a person to attend a conference"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "11067c62a337ae67c580626a4eec9dcc989fda822aebc81a01d278ca2f6094c3" ;
    values:partOf concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-246 ;
    cof:pageNumber "489"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "FWC may provide assistance to bargaining representatives." ;
